# Cross-device save sync (optional).
#
# Leave unset and the game runs entirely on local storage, exactly as it does today:
# the sync layer short-circuits and nothing is sent anywhere.
#
# Set it to a REST slot that supports two verbs on /<playerId>:
#   GET  -> 200 with the save payload, or 404 when the slot is empty
#   PUT  -> stores the JSON body
# A Supabase edge function, a Firebase callable behind a rewrite, or any small
# server all work; the game does not care which.
#
# VITE_SYNC_ENDPOINT=https://your-backend.example/saves

# Rewarded adverts (optional).
#
# Leave unset and no advert surface is rendered at all: the shop looks exactly as it
# does today and no ad SDK is loaded. Watching an advert is never required to progress —
# every offer is a power-up that can also simply be bought with coins.
#
# To activate you need an AdMob account, a rewarded ad unit id, and the plugin:
#   npm i @capacitor-community/admob && npx cap sync
#
# VITE_ADMOB_REWARDED_ID=ca-app-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/XXXXXXXXXX

# Anonymous gameplay analytics (optional).
#
# Leave unset and the analytics toggle does not even appear in Settings: no queue is
# written and nothing is transmitted. When set, the feature is still off until the
# player opts in, which is what keeps the privacy policy's default guarantee true.
#
# Receives POST { events: [...] } with no identifier of any kind — see PRIVACY_POLICY.md
# section 5.1 for exactly what a record contains.
#
# If VITE_SYNC_ENDPOINT is set and this is not, <sync endpoint>/telemetry is used, so one
# small server can serve both.
#
# VITE_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT=https://your-backend.example/telemetry
